course: dictionary
lesson: 4259
title: Gratefulness: the thank-you feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gratefulness is the feeling of being thankful and glad. You feel it when someone does something kind for you, or when you notice a good thing in your life. The sentence «disappointment and gratefulness can sit side by side» tells you that two feelings can be there at the same time.
explain: The sentence shows that both feelings are real and normal. The girl was let down about her dog dream, but she was also glad for the small things she had. Check the meaning by swapping in a simple word, like thankfulness, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Gratefulness is a noun, a name for a feeling. The ending -ness turns a describing word into a name, so grateful becomes gratefulness. Grateful is the describing word you use in a sentence like «I am grateful for your help.»
explain: People show gratefulness in many ways, such as saying thank you, keeping a gratitude journal, or giving thanks in prayer. Stories also show it through a character's kindness and good manners.
fact: Gratefulness means the feeling of being thankful and glad.
fact: Gratefulness is a noun, a name for a feeling, and it is uncountable, so you do not say "a gratefulness".
fact: The word comes from «grateful», which means thankful, with the ending -ness added.
fact: Some families and classes keep a gratitude journal, where they write down good things to be thankful for.
fact: In church, Christians show gratefulness to God by giving thanks in prayer.
exercise: In «disappointment and gratefulness can sit side by side», what does gratefulness mean? | A place where you sit to rest | The name of a dog | *The feeling of being thankful and glad | The feeling of being angry at someone
exercise: Gratefulness is a name for a feeling. Which describing word does it come from? | gratefulness | side | *grateful | normal
exercise: Which is a good way to show gratefulness? | Shouting when something goes wrong | Ignoring the good things in your life | *Saying thank you to someone who helped you | Refusing to say anything kind
test: In «disappointment and gratefulness can sit side by side», why are both feelings normal? | They mean exactly the same thing | *They can both be felt at the same time | They are both kinds of weather | Only grown-ups can feel gratefulness
test: In «learning about hamsters made room for the small one she had», what is the small one? | The big dream | A hamster she had to give back | *A small thing she was thankful for | Mum pretending
exam: Which sentence is the best example of gratefulness? | I was cross because nobody came to my party | I lost my pencil case | *Thank you, Gran, for making my favourite soup when I was ill | The bus was late again today
